#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:128
msgid "Getting started"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:130
msgid "Quick start (5 minutes)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:133
msgid "Go to <strong>AdFlow → Settings → General</strong> and paste your AdSense Publisher ID (<code>pub-1234567890123456</code> - the <code>ca-pub-</code> form works too)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:134
msgid "Turn on <strong>Auto Ads</strong> if you want Google to place ads for you, or leave it off and place ads yourself."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:135
msgid "Open <strong>Settings → ads.txt</strong> and turn it on, so AdSense stops warning \"Earnings at risk\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:136
msgid "Create an ad unit under <strong>AdFlow → Ad Units → Add</strong> with the slot ID from AdSense, then put it in a placement (AdFlow → Placements) or add the \"AdFlow Ad\" block to a post."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:137
msgid "Check the <strong>Dashboard</strong>: it lists anything that could stop ads from showing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:139
msgid "New AdSense accounts can take a few days to show ads. Empty spaces during that time are normal."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:141
msgid "Open Settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:142
msgid "Open Dashboard"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:147
msgid "Find your Publisher ID and ad slot IDs"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:149
msgid "<strong>Publisher ID:</strong> in AdSense, open Account → Settings → Account information. It looks like <code>pub-1234567890123456</code>."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:150
msgid "<strong>Ad slot ID:</strong> in AdSense, open Ads → By ad unit, create a unit (Display, In-feed, In-article or Multiplex) and copy the number after <code>data-ad-slot</code> in the code Google shows you."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:151
msgid "In-feed ads also have a <strong>layout key</strong> (<code>data-ad-layout-key</code>); copy it into the ad unit too."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:152
msgid "Google: create a display ad unit"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:158
msgid "Auto Ads let Google choose where ads go. Turn them on under Settings → General. You can exclude post types (e.g. products) and single pages by ID, and hide ads from logged-in administrators so you never click your own ads."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:159
msgid "Which formats Auto Ads use (anchor, vignette, in-page) is set in your AdSense account under Ads → By site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:160
msgid "You can combine Auto Ads with your own placements. Google fills the rest of the page around them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:161
msgid "<strong>Manual ads</strong> (placements, the block, widgets and shortcodes) have their own <em>Pages without manual ads</em> setting under Settings → General → Manual ads. Pick content types, or list posts and pages by ID, and no manual ad shows there, including ads in sidebar widgets. The two settings are independent, so a page can keep Auto Ads and drop manual ads, or the other way round."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:167
msgid "ads.txt tells buyers you are allowed to sell ads on your site. Without it, AdSense shows \"Earnings at risk\". Turn it on under <strong>Settings → ads.txt</strong>: AdFlow serves the Google line from your Publisher ID and any extra lines you add for other networks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:168
msgid "The <strong>Check live file</strong> button fetches <code>/ads.txt</code> the way Google does. If a physical ads.txt file exists in your site root, it wins - delete it or copy its lines into AdFlow."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:169
msgid "Open ads.txt settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:174
msgid "Ads & placements"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:178
msgid "An ad unit is an ad you set up once and reuse everywhere: in placements, the block, the widget and shortcodes. Change it once and every place updates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:180
msgid "<strong>Google AdSense:</strong> Display, In-article, In-feed and Multiplex, using the same ad code attributes Google gives you. A block with no saved unit gets the code for its type too."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:181
msgid "<strong>Your own ads:</strong> Image banner, Text ad, Custom code (any network, HTML/JS - needs the \"unfiltered HTML\" permission)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:182
msgid "<strong>Rotation group:</strong> several ads take turns."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:183
msgid "<strong>Google Ad Manager (GPT)</strong> - with AdFlow Pro."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:185
msgid "The <strong>Will this ad show?</strong> box on each ad lists everything that could stop it: missing Publisher ID or slot, schedule, a group with nothing left to show, waiting for consent, targeting, placement."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:186
msgid "Add an ad unit"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:190
msgid "Block, widget & shortcodes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:192
msgid "<strong>Block:</strong> add the \"AdFlow Ad\" block in the editor and pick an ad unit. <strong>Widget:</strong> Appearance → Widgets → \"AdFlow Ad\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:194
msgid "Shortcodes from earlier versions keep working:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:196
msgid "Optional attributes: <code>style</code> and <code>class</code>."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:200
msgid "Automatic placements"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:202
msgid "Placements insert an ad unit into every post without editing posts: <strong>before content</strong>, <strong>after paragraph N</strong> and <strong>after content</strong>, for the post types you choose. Posts shorter than N paragraphs are skipped."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:203
msgid "Put a rotation group in a placement to rotate several ads in the same spot."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:204
#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:218
msgid "Open Placements"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:210
msgid "Under <strong>AdFlow → Placements → More ads inside posts</strong>, choose <strong>Add an ad</strong> as often as you need. Each one has its own ad unit, post types and conditions, and starts working once you save."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:212
msgid "<strong>Every few paragraphs</strong>: for example every 4 paragraphs, at most 3 per post. Never after the last paragraph."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:213
msgid "<strong>After one paragraph</strong>: a second, third or fourth fixed spot."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:214
msgid "<strong>Before or after an HTML element</strong>: see below."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:216
msgid "Posts shorter than <em>Skip posts shorter than</em> are left alone. Two ads are never adjacent: an extra ad is skipped when any other ad, including one you added by hand, is closer than two paragraphs. Developers can change that distance with <code>adflow_content_slot_min_spacing</code>."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:217
msgid "Statistics for your own ads record each extra ad separately, and each ad counts towards the AdFlow Pro limit on ads per page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:224
msgid "Use this when the spot is not about paragraphs, for example after the second heading. Add an ad, choose <strong>Before or after an HTML element</strong>, then enter a CSS selector such as <code>.entry-content h2</code> and which match to use (2 = the second one)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:225
msgid "The page holds the ad in an inert template and the browser moves it into place, so it works on cached pages. If the element is not on a page, nothing shows and no ad is requested. AdSense units use Google's normal code. Your own custom code runs when it is inserted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:226
msgid "<strong>Reserve height</strong> keeps room for the ad so text does not jump when it loads (default 250 px; 0 for none). It goes away when AdSense reports no ad to show."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:227
msgid "Selectors depend on your theme and may need changing if you switch themes. An ad placed outside your content area must still follow your ad network's rules."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:231
msgid "Conditions: device, category, tag, posts, language"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:233
msgid "Every placement has a <strong>Conditions</strong> section. Leave it empty to show everywhere. An ad must match every condition you set."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:235
msgid "<strong>Device</strong>: mobile only, or tablet and desktop only. Mobile means a screen up to 767 px wide. It is decided in the browser, so it works behind page caches, and no ad is requested on the other device. With AdFlow Pro active, this field is in its Targeting section."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:236
msgid "<strong>Categories and tags</strong>: only posts with one of the chosen terms. With AdFlow Pro active, categories are in its Targeting section."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:237
msgid "<strong>Only on / never on these posts or pages</strong>: search by title or ID."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:238
msgid "<strong>Languages</strong>: shown when Polylang or WPML is active."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:243
msgid "Turn ads off on one post or page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:245
msgid "Users who can manage ads see an <strong>AdFlow Ads</strong> box in the editor sidebar of every public post type: <em>No ads</em>, <em>No Auto Ads</em> and <em>No manual ads</em> on that page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:246
msgid "To do it from one place, use <em>Pages without Auto Ads</em> and <em>Pages without manual ads</em> under Settings → General. Search for a post or page by title, or type its ID as before."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:250
msgid "Elementor and Bricks"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:252
msgid "Search for <strong>AdFlow Ad</strong> in the Elementor or Bricks elements panel, add it and choose a saved ad unit. The editor shows a stand-in box, so ads do not load or count while you design. The ad unit follows all your rules on the live page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:256
msgid "Multilingual sites: Polylang and WPML"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:258
msgid "With Polylang or WPML active, each placement can be limited to chosen languages under <strong>Conditions</strong>. The simplest way to run per-language ads is one placement per language."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:259
msgid "AdFlow also ships a <code>wpml-config.xml</code>: if you turn on translation for Ad Units in your language plugin, a placement shows the translation of its ad unit in each language. A headline, text, button, image text and link can then differ per language. Ad units are not made translatable automatically, because ads that already run have no language set."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:263
msgid "More placements: mid-article, between posts, sticky, popup, WooCommerce"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:267
msgid "<strong>Middle of the article (after X%)</strong> - scales with post length."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:268
msgid "<strong>Between posts</strong> - every N posts on home, category, tag and search pages (classic and block themes)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:269
msgid "<strong>Before comments</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:270
msgid "<strong>Sticky anchor</strong> - a small bar at the bottom that visitors can close. AdSense display units are requested at a fixed size (320x50 on phones, 728x90 on larger screens); other AdSense unit types do not show in it. The page keeps room for it while it shows, and it collapses when Google has no ad."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:271
msgid "<strong>Popup</strong> - for sponsor banners and other networks, after a delay or scroll depth, once per visitor per N days. Google does not allow AdSense in popups, so AdSense units are never shown there."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:272
msgid "<strong>WooCommerce</strong> - above the product grid, below the product summary, after add-to-cart."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:274
msgid "<strong>Sticky sidebar:</strong> turn on \"Keep in view while scrolling\" on an ad unit and place it last in your sidebar. On desktop it stays visible while visitors read."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:278
msgid "Targeting, scheduling & A/B tests"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:281
msgid "Each placement can be limited by <strong>device</strong> (mobile/desktop), <strong>visitor</strong> (logged in/out), <strong>traffic source</strong> (search engines or not), <strong>categories</strong>, <strong>post age</strong> and <strong>start/end dates</strong>. Device and traffic rules run in the browser, so they work with page caching - and an ad that should not show never requests an ad from Google."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:282
msgid "<strong>A/B rotation:</strong> add extra ad units to a placement. The browser picks one per page view, so it also works on cached pages. The Earnings screen compares only the units in the same test, shows the sample size and names a winner only when each unit has at least 1,000 impressions and 10 clicks and the gap is larger than chance."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:286
msgid "Google Ad Manager (GPT) units"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:289
msgid "Choose the type \"Google Ad Manager (GPT)\" and enter the <strong>ad unit path</strong> (<code>/1234567/sidebar</code>, from Ad Manager → Inventory → Ad units → Tags), the <strong>sizes</strong> (<code>300x250, 336x280, fluid</code>) and optional <strong>mobile sizes</strong> for screens under 768px."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:290
msgid "<strong>Key-values</strong> (one <code>key=value</code> per line) target line items. Macros: <code>{post_id}</code>, <code>{post_type}</code>, <code>{category}</code>, <code>{placement}</code>."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:292
msgid "GPT loads once, asynchronously, only on pages that show such a unit. Whether a slot fills depends on your line items."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:297
msgid "Your own ads & selling"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:299
msgid "Banners, text ads and custom code"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:301
msgid "Run sponsor, affiliate or house ads next to AdSense. Image banners come from the Media Library; text ads have a headline, text and button. Links get <code>rel=\"sponsored\"</code> (add nofollow if you like) and can open in a new tab."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:303
msgid "<strong>Disclosure label:</strong> \"Sponsored\" or \"Advertisement\" above the ad - laws in many countries require it for paid ads."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:304
msgid "<strong>Schedule:</strong> start and end date and time (your site's time zone). Cached pages follow it too: the ad appears at the start, and at the end it goes away and its AdSense fallback appears. This takes JavaScript and uses the visitor's clock."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:305
msgid "<strong>When not running:</strong> show an AdSense unit instead, so the space keeps earning."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:306
msgid "Own ads use neutral class names, so ad blockers are less likely to hide them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:308
msgid "Destination links may contain tracking macros: <code>{ad_id}</code>, <code>{placement}</code>, <code>{site}</code>, <code>{cachebuster}</code>."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:312
msgid "Rotation groups"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:314
msgid "A rotation group shows one of its ads per page view: <strong>weighted</strong> (an ad with weight 3 shows three times as often as weight 1) or <strong>in order</strong>. The choice is made in the browser, so it works with page caching."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:315
msgid "Only ads that may show right now take part: scheduled, capped, out-of-hours or other-country ads are skipped. Mix sponsor ads with an AdSense unit so the spot is never empty."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:319
msgid "Sell ads directly (self-serve)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:323
msgid "Create a rotation group (Ad Units → Add → Rotation group) and put it in a placement."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:324
msgid "Under <strong>Settings → Sell ads</strong>, add a package: name, banner or text, size, days, price and your payment link (a Stripe Payment Link, PayPal.me or any checkout)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:325
msgid "Create an \"Advertise with us\" page with the shortcode <code>[adflow_advertise]</code>."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:326
msgid "Advertisers choose a package, upload their banner or write a text ad, and pay with your link (the order number is passed as <code>?order=</code>)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:327
msgid "Orders wait under <strong>Ad Units → Pending</strong>. Check the creative and payment (\"Mark as paid\"), then Publish: the ad joins the package's group for the paid days and stops by itself. The advertiser receives a live report link and weekly emails."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:329
msgid "No card data ever reaches your site. The form works on cached pages and is protected against spam."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:333
msgid "Advertiser reports, emails & pricing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:337
msgid "<strong>Advertiser details & campaign price</strong> on each own ad; the sponsor eCPM is shown next to your AdSense RPM."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:338
msgid "<strong>Report link:</strong> a read-only page with the ad's statistics - no login. Create or turn it off in the ad's sidebar."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:339
msgid "<strong>Performance emails:</strong> weekly (Mondays) or monthly (the 1st) to the advertiser. \"Email me a preview\" shows what they get."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:340
msgid "<strong>Expiry reminders</strong> to you (and optionally the advertiser) 7 days before and when a campaign ends."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:341
msgid "<strong>Frequency cap</strong> (impressions per visitor per day) and <strong>dayparting</strong> (days and hours)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:342
msgid "<strong>Country targeting:</strong> \"Only in\" or \"Everywhere except\" a list of country codes. The country comes from Cloudflare or your host, or from the optional free country database (Countries field → \"Use the free country database\")."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:348
msgid "Reports & earnings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:350
msgid "How statistics are counted"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:352
msgid "AdFlow counts impressions, viewable impressions and clicks of your own ads using industry (IAB/MRC) definitions:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:354
msgid "<strong>Impression</strong> - the ad was actually displayed (for banners: the image loaded). Hidden, prefetched and prerendered pages do not count."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:355
msgid "<strong>Viewable</strong> - at least half of the ad was on screen for one continuous second."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:356
msgid "<strong>Click</strong> - a link in the ad was opened; a scroll that starts on the ad is not a click."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:357
msgid "<strong>Not counted</strong> - bots, headless browsers, link previews and logged-in administrators."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:359
msgid "Reports store daily totals only - no IP addresses or visitor IDs - it sets no cookies and it works with page caching. To stop abuse of the counter, a one-way number that many visitors share is kept for up to a day; it cannot be turned back into an address."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:361
msgid "These numbers are estimates, not audited figures. The counter has to be public, so someone determined can still add to it. AdFlow makes that harder: requests need a token from your pages and must not come from another site, each visitor address has a limit per minute, unknown placements are ignored, and a day's clicks on an ad cannot pass its impressions. Extra clicks are set aside and shown in Reports. If all your visitors reach WordPress through one proxy address, add its address with the adflow_trusted_proxies filter (Cloudflare and private addresses are already known) or raise adflow_stats_rate_limit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:363
msgid "Under Settings → Tracking you can wait for statistics consent, count clicks through a redirect link instead, and choose how long data is kept."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:364
msgid "AdSense statistics come from Google; AdFlow does not count AdSense impressions itself."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:365
msgid "Open Reports"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:365
msgid "Tracking settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:369
msgid "Full reports, CSV, REST API & WP-CLI"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:372
msgid "Custom date ranges, breakdowns by placement, device and advertiser, and CSV export on the Reports screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:374
msgid "Authenticate the REST API with an Application Password (Users → Profile) of a user who may view reports."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:378
#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-upsell.php:146
msgid "AdSense earnings in WordPress"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:381
msgid "Connect your Google account under <strong>AdFlow → Earnings</strong> to see today, yesterday, this month, page RPM, clicks, top pages and per-unit earnings - plus a dashboard widget. AdFlow only asks for read-only access to AdSense reports. Until one-click sign-in is available, you first set up your own free Google Cloud project once (about 10 to 15 minutes; the steps are on that screen). Your site needs HTTPS, and Google shows an \"unverified app\" warning for your own project: choose Advanced and continue."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:386
msgid "Privacy, safety & team"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:388
msgid "GDPR: Consent Mode v2 & loading ads after consent"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:390
msgid "Google requires consent before personalised ads in the EEA, UK and Switzerland. Show the consent message with AdSense's own \"Privacy & messaging\" (a Google-certified TCF message) or a consent plugin such as Complianz, CookieYes or Cookiebot. A plugin cannot make a site compliant on its own: AdFlow makes your ads respect the answer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:392
msgid "<strong>Load ads after consent</strong> - other networks' code and Ad Manager slots load only after the visitor agrees to advertising. The AdSense library loads once a TCF message is answered, because Google reads the choice itself; with other tools, only after the visitor agrees. No timer ever releases ads. Your own banners and text ads use no cookies and show straight away."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:393
msgid "<strong>Where the answer comes from</strong> - an IAB TCF message, the WP Consent API with a plugin that supports it, CookieYes, Complianz or Cookiebot. The Privacy tab warns if your tool is none of these; ads then stay held. Your tool can release them by calling <code>window.afxConsent.grant()</code> from its \"accepted\" callback."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:394
msgid "<strong>AdSense's own consent message</strong> - it only reaches the page with the AdSense library, so turning this on loads the library at once. If the message is not set up in AdSense, nobody is asked. Other networks' code still waits. With no consent plugin it starts on; with one it starts off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:395
msgid "<strong>Google Consent Mode v2</strong> - tells Google tags consent is \"denied\" until the visitor agrees and passes on their choice (from the WP Consent API, CookieYes, Complianz or Cookiebot). Use it when your banner is not a Google-certified TCF message."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:396
msgid "<strong>Other countries</strong> - AdFlow cannot tell where a visitor is, so they wait too unless the consent tool says consent is not needed for them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:398
msgid "Open Privacy & consent"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:402
msgid "AMP pages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:404
msgid "With the official AMP plugin, AdSense units print Google's <code>amp-ad</code> code and Auto Ads print <code>amp-auto-ads</code>. The AMP plugin adds the scripts they need."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:406
msgid "Your own banners and text ads show as plain markup, without statistics, because AMP allows no custom scripts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:407
msgid "Rotation groups show one ad, chosen on the server. A page cache keeps that choice until it is refreshed. The same goes for schedules."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:408
msgid "Custom code shows only if it contains an AMP element such as <code>amp-ad</code>. Pro's Ad Manager units and popup and sticky formats do not show."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:409
msgid "With \"Load ads after consent\" on, AdSense ads and Auto Ads are left out of AMP pages, because AMP pages cannot wait for AdFlow's consent check."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:414
msgid "Invalid-click protection & ad limits"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:417
msgid "Stops showing ads to a visitor who clicks ads too often (e.g. 3 clicks in 24 hours → no ads for 7 days). Flagged visitors never load the AdSense script, so no ad is ever hidden - hiding ads breaks AdSense policy. It reduces risk; no tool can guarantee Google's decisions."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:418
msgid "<strong>Check it works:</strong> never click your own live ads, because Google treats that as invalid activity. Open a page, choose AdFlow → Inspect ads on this page in the toolbar, and use <strong>Test with a dummy ad</strong>. The note shows the clicks seen on the dummy frame and the real clicks counted in this browser, and <strong>Reset this browser</strong> clears them. Flagged visitors stop getting Google ads; your sponsors' banner and text ads still show to them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:419
msgid "Also on Settings → Click protection: <strong>Max manual ads per page</strong> and a polite <strong>ad-blocker message</strong>. Settings → Performance: <strong>lazy loading</strong>; each ad unit: <strong>reserved height</strong> against layout shift."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:423
msgid "Roles, permissions & approvals"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:425
msgid "Under <strong>Settings → Access</strong>, give other roles \"Create & edit ads\", \"Publish ads (no review)\" and \"View reports\". Administrators always have full access; settings stay with administrators."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:426
msgid "<strong>Approval workflow:</strong> someone who may create but not publish ads gets \"Submit for Review\". Everyone who may publish is emailed, and the Dashboard shows the ads waiting."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-google-adsense-docs.php:427
msgid "Open Access"
msgstr ""

